{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "SnapshotInterpolationBuffer, replayed step by step: each add gives the sample's server time, local arrival, x and x velocity (float32 bits, velocity null when absent) and the result; each frame gives the local time, render time, mode, x, target delay and playback offset after the frame. Delay: the longer of the interval estimate and the largest gap between buffered samples, plus three jitters, clamped to 80-350 ms. The playback offset (render time minus local time) moves toward offset minus delay by at most 10% of elapsed local time, then the render time is floored at the last render time and, for a full buffer, at the oldest sample, and the playback offset follows the floored render time. Y and z are zero and rotations identity.",
